{
  "rationale": "Race evidence from iteration 1 (entityR2A): all 60 trials ended off_track, with progress 0.04 to 0.15, max_error at 0.0611 to 0.0637 (the 0.06 m limit plus a little), rms_error about 0.02 to 0.03, and about one line-loss event per run. Steering oscillation stayed low (0.10 to 0.14), so the robot is not jittering. It drifts steadily outward and loses the tape, and the sensor geometry is the likely cause. With sensors spanning only x = +/-0.03 m, the outer sensors stop seeing the 25 mm tape once the centre-line offset passes about 0.045 to 0.05 m (half-tape 0.0125 m plus footprint). The robot then loses the line before it reaches the 0.06 m off-track limit. Changes: widen the array to 7 sensors spanning x = +/-0.06 m at 0.02 m spacing, so the line stays visible to offsets of about 0.07 to 0.08 m. Enlarge the footprint to 0.016 m, which still fits within the 25 mm tape and gives a smoother reading. Keep the sensors at y = 0.06 m, since that lookahead was not shown to hurt. Raise wheel_radius from 0.03 to 0.035 m. For a given wheel rotation rate, this raises ground speed, which helps the 3 s finish requirement (about 1.5 m/s average). Keep wheel_track 0.10 m, mass 0.6 kg, body_length 0.14 m and body_width 0.12 m. Body_width changes nothing here: its contribution is below the 0.06 m floor across the whole allowed range. Expected result: fewer line-loss events, max_error held below the off-track limit on bends, and higher progress on the s-bend and slalom. Completion is still uncertain, and it depends on whether the controller can use the wider signal.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.06, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": -0.04, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": 0.04, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": 0.06, "y": 0.06}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.016,
    "wheel_track": 0.10,
    "wheel_radius": 0.035,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.14,
    "mass": 0.6
  },
  "intent": "Test the hypothesis that the robot loses the line at offsets of about 0.045 to 0.05 m, because the +/-0.03 m sensor span stops seeing the tape before the off-track limit. Changes from iteration 1: sensor span widened to +/-0.06 m with 7 sensors at 0.02 m spacing; sensor footprint 0.012 to 0.016 m; wheel_radius 0.03 to 0.035 m for more ground speed per wheel rotation. Expected result: line_loss_events fall toward 0, max_error stays below 0.06 on the s-bend, and progress rises on the oval and slalom. Controller weights should be set to match the wider array (for example proportional to x, with 7 entries).",
  "feedback_request": {
    "measurements": ["completion", "progress", "completion_time", "rms_error", "max_error", "line_loss_events", "steering_oscillation", "control_effort", "noise_robustness", "controller_errors"]
  },
  "learning": "Next iteration, check: (a) whether line_loss_events drop from about 1 per run to near 0, which would confirm the narrow-span hypothesis; (b) whether max_error still reaches 0.06, which would mean turn authority rather than sensing is the limit; (c) whether progress moves on the s-bend, the sharpest track; (d) whether the larger wheel radius raises completion_time or steering_oscillation. Ask the Integrator whether the 7-sensor signal saturates at the array edges, and what sensor_weights they used."
}
